From: "Engineering Agent (Chat 2)" <agent@ascentt.dev>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 13:43:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Conference scheduling, global season completion, background
 cups (for review, not merged)

Implements three engine changes, staged for independent review by Chat 1
(lead review) and Chat 3 (Git/QA review). NOT merged into main.

1. Global season completion: getCurrentMatchday now scans all 8 league
   tiers instead of only the user's own tier, fixing silent fixture
   truncation. isWorldSeasonComplete added, requiring all 3 domestic cups
   done as well before a season can roll over.

2. MLS / USL Championship conference-based scheduling, replacing the
   generic round-robin previously used for all 4 USA tiers:
   - MLS: 34 games per club, exactly 17 home / 17 away (provably exact
     via a circulant construction, not an approximation), 28 intra-
     conference + 6 cross-conference games, 15 East / 15 West.
   - USLC: 30 games per club, real-world-matching 7-clubs-at-6 /
     6-clubs-at-5 cross-conference split for the 13-club East side, all
     12 West clubs at 6 cross games via 2 extra intra-conference games
     each.
   - USL1 restored to double round-robin (was incorrectly downgraded to
     single-leg every season after season 1). USL2 left unchanged as an
     intentional simplification.
   - Persistent geoConference field (permanent geographic identity,
     assigned once, survives promotion/relegation through the whole USA
     pyramid) kept separate from seasonal `conference` (this season's
     actual placement).
   - Tier-scoped border-market lists (MLS, USLC, USL1, USL2 -- each
     independent) used only as a last-resort, deterministic tie-break
     when conference-size constraints force a temporary crossover.

3. Background cups: US Open Cup, FA Cup, and EFL Cup now all run every
   season regardless of which pyramid the user is playing in (previously
   the non-user side's cup never progressed at all). UI recap popups
   remain scoped to the user's own side.

Files changed: src/App.jsx, src/data/rosters.js, src/engine/constants.js,
src/engine/cups.js, src/engine/leagueSim.js, src/engine/worldBuild.js,
src/engine/scheduling.js (new).

Tested via a headless Node harness driving the real engine modules
directly: season/cup lifecycle across all 8 starting tiers, a 15-season
pure-AI regression, exact schedule-shape verification, 8 geographic-
identity scenarios, and cross-tier border-list isolation. This has NOT
been manually/UI tested and is not being represented as production-ready.
